Reviewed `src/blog/people/drafts/Hunter-Biden.md` and appended a `FRESH EYES REVIEW (2026-07-25)` block at the bottom (the existing `REVIEWER NOTES` block is preserved above it). No body edits.

**The two biggest issues:**

1. **Navy Joan Roberts is completely absent** — and the draft's entire thesis is that this is a man who confesses everything. He denied paternity of a daughter born in 2018, was established as her father by an Arkansas court in January 2020, fought child support for years, settled in June 2023 by offering paintings, and in January 2026 the case was reopened over claims he ghosted her. A reader who knows this hits the *"most transparent motherf***er"* pull-quote and stops believing the piece. It's either the strongest test the Type 4 call survives — the one record he refused to author — or the hole that sinks it. Staying silent is the only option that doesn't work.

2. **The tax case is missing entirely.** The draft says "convicted on three felony counts" and stops. He also pleaded guilty to nine tax charges in LA on September 5, 2024, hours before jury selection, after the July 2023 plea deal collapsed in open court. Same pardon wiped both. Its absence makes the legal spine look thinner than it was.

The strongest missing *scene* is the January 10, 2024 contempt hearing — he refused the closed-door deposition, then physically walked in and sat in the front row while they voted on holding him in contempt. That's the purest "you will look at me" moment in the record and it would carry the piece's weakest section.

Sources: [WaPo — Navy Roberts acknowledgment](https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2023/07/28/biden-hunter-granddaughter-navy-roberts/), [AOL — paternity case reopened](https://www.aol.com/articles/hunter-biden-accused-ghosting-daughter-213711559.html), [CNN — tax guilty plea](https://www.cnn.com/2024/09/05/politics/hunter-biden-case), [NPR — surprise contempt-hearing appearance](https://www.npr.org/2024/01/10/1224021556/hunter-biden-surprise-contempt-appearance)
